{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1530498-review-dark-prince-by-keith-herber-the-first-vtm-novel","id":1530498,"title":"Review - Dark Prince by Keith Herber - The first VTM novel","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-02-10T16:18:24-08:00","id":1530498,"title":"Review - Dark Prince by Keith Herber - The first VTM novel","content":"[link deleted]<br /> <br /> DARK PRINCE by Keith Herber is the first full-length novel for the World of Darkness and, more specifically, VAMPIRE: THE MASQUERADE setting. It was published in 1994 and introduced the character of Vannevar Thomas. It also imagined a complicated interlocking web of undead politics taking place behind closed doors in San Fransisco.<br /> <br /> Dark Prince would have a single sequel in PRINCE OF THE CITY before having a lot of its lore retconned or ignored in SAN FRANSISCO BY NIGHT. Later, it would be recanonized with Jason Carl\u2019s fantastic LA BY NIGHT incorporating some of the characters as well as their lore. The book would be out of print for about two decades, not even available on RPGNow in PDF form, until Crossroad Press re-released it in 2024.<br /> <br /> With that history lesson out of the way, I\u2019m going to admit my horrible bias towards this book. I read this book when it first came out in 1994 and would buy it used a couple of more times. It\u2019s not just a good <i>Vampire: The Masquerade</i> story or even a good vampire story but a good novel period. It\u2019s gritty, dark, and incorporates all of the weirdness of the World of Darkness without requiring any knowledge of the setting beforehand.<br /> <br /> Indeed, that is probably my main selling point for <i>Dark Prince</i>. The lore of tabletop RPGs, especially the World of Darkness, is often impenetrable to outsiders. You either get too much of it and can\u2019t enjoy it unless you\u2019re already a player like the Clan Novels or they just go with the vampire horror element ala WALK AMONG US and you don\u2019t have enough to differentiate it. Here, the story manages to capture the interlocking web of politics, horror, and characterization to make a perfect example of what <i>Vampire: The Masquerade</i> should be. Just one small problem: the main character is a complete scumbag. Another is, well, let\u2019s just say this isn\u2019t necessarily the most culturally sensitive book in the world either.<br /> <br /> The premise is San Fransisco in 1994 where a particularly scummy Caitiff vampire named Sullivan is intimidating prostitutes under his control and shaking them down for twenties. Sullivan works for the Family, a group of Chinese vampires who have been working the docks since the 19th century and don\u2019t seem to follow the Cainite clan structure but are still able to make their own. Sullivan is neither particularly smart nor insightful but he\u2019s doggedly loyal. So much so that the Family has kept him on despite the fact they only Embraced him as an intermediary with the white criminal element.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately, for Sullivan, Kindred power games don\u2019t care if you\u2019re loyal or not and he\u2019s soon set up as a traitor to the mysterious Grandfather. Sullivan finds himself bouncing from one faction to the next in San Fransisco, trying to find someone who will protect him from his sire. This includes the Anarchs, Prince, Primogen, old friends, and even older enemies. Sullivan soon finds out that his banal street level of evil has nothing on elder vampires or the Sabbat. He also finds himself shamed by vampires who actually tried to help others during the AIDS crisis among other human tragedies.<br /> <br /> <i>Dark Prince</i> knows how to keep a careful balance between lore and character development. Garou, hunters, a frigging Bane, and (arguably) the Kuei-Jin show up in the book but you\u2019re never overwhelmed. The focus is entirely on Sullivan realizing he\u2019s wasted his vampire life and debating whether or not he should try to become a better person or pursue something more meaningful than being the exact sort of low level scum he\u2019s been for a century. As you might guess, power and prestige don\u2019t go well with personal growth. Neither does maintaining any sense of freedom or command over your own destiny.<br /> <br /> I really recommend this book if you want to get started in the World of Darkness but also note that, well, the lead is a scummy pimp who only begins to become someone you don\u2019t want to see staked for the sun later on. Also, there\u2019s the koala scene. Let\u2019s just say that the Sabbat don\u2019t get any sympathy in this book. They\u2019re very much of the irredeemable monster interpretation even if they talk a good game about freedom. Still, it\u2019s got a lot of drama and the ending is superb. I\u2019m glad it\u2019s available back in print after twenty years.<br /> <br /> [link deleted]","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":152,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer","user":"The Gentleman Gamer","date":". 02-12-2024, 12:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-10T20:55:47-08:00","id":1530530,"title":"","content":"Oh, i remember that one - sort of. A friend of mine bought it and would use some elements and characters in his own game, if memory tricks me not.<br /> The one i did manage to get a copy from was the <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/The_Beast_Within\" target=\"_blank\">Beast Within</a> anthology, that had some connections and referenced a number of characters.<br /> <br /> (Was that the one with a Qing Dynasty princess turned Cleopatra as the matriarch of a community of undead exiles in the undercity/chinatown's made from the buried ruins of the 1906 earthquake? If so, pardon the spoiler)<br /> <br /> <br /> And on the subject of cultural sensitivity, it's complicated - from one side, as you said, the book came in '94, barely 5 years after <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Black_Rain_(1989_American_film)\" target=\"_blank\">Black Rain</a> and <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kinjite:_Forbidden_Subjects\" target=\"_blank\">Kinjite</a> hit the big screen, not to mention a slew of clones &amp; derivatives, so in that aspect it's a product of influences, good &amp; bad, of its time.<br /> <br /> On another, it's terribly easy to forget that the boom of martial arts and asian culture in western media in the mid- to late '70s, less than a generation before, was the incidental fruit of a major human exodus tied into <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cultural_Revolution\" target=\"_blank\">one unfortunate event</a> not so far back in time, with ties in <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Great_Chinese_Famine\" target=\"_blank\">other</a> just as <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Great_Leap_Forward\" target=\"_blank\">terrible ones</a>. So it all depends on frame of reference - one person's cultural insensitive landscape can be another's lens in personal perspectives that time and media are sometimes too effective at washing out the horror off.<br /> <br /> Also, KotE while trying to sell itself as a positive and heroic take could end up as bad if not worse at times through the &quot;kuei-jin&quot; (<i>sic</i>) lore-enforced propensity to channel the worse of Garou jingoistic antagonism for kindred. And the less said about their move into the American West Coast (did someone really call that <i>Great Leap Forward</i>?!), the better... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> On an aside, i think Sullivan was meant to be some sort of &quot;positive counter-example&quot; to the average beginning PC, so to speak. &quot;<i>If a completely awful person like this guy here can find room to change and perhaps grow itself into a halfway decent human being, so can you</i>!&quot;, brand of &quot;rags to riches or redemption?&quot; storyline to compare and contrast oneself with, if that makes sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-10T21:26:57-08:00","id":1530532,"title":"","content":"I actually feel like DARK PRINCE has a lot more interesting take on things than many later installments of Vampire: The Masquerade. It may fall into stereotype at times with the fanatical Spanish Brujah, sinister Chinese crime lord, and so on but the fact is that it actually is trying to celebrate the complicated cultural history and diversity of San Fransisco. This is a book that may have some cringe-y characters but is also a book with Hispanic, Chinese, gay, straight, Black, and white characters. How many other books can you say do have that kind of representation?<br /> <br /> In a very real way, I feel like this book also does a decent job of reflecting how Fifth Edition should be played. It's a gritty street level series of adventures and events with a protagonist who is struggling against his Beast as well as the complicated politics of Kindred society.<br /> <br /> Sullivan doesn't WANT to scheme or do anything other than loyally serve. But loyalty means nothing if there's more to be had by betraying YOU.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 02-11-2024, 02:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-10T22:36:46-08:00","id":1530535,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1530498-review-dark-prince-by-keith-herber-the-first-vtm-novel?p=1530532#post1530532\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I actually feel like DARK DESTINY has a lot more interesting take on things than many later installments of Vampire: The Masquerade. It may fall into stereotype at times with the fanatical Spanish Brujah, sinister Chinese crime lord, and so on but the fact is that it actually is trying to celebrate the complicated cultural history and diversity of San Fransisco. This is a book that may have some cringe-y characters but is also a book with Hispanic, Chinese, gay, straight, Black, and white characters. How many other books can you say do have that kind of representation?</div> </div> </div> </div>Wasn't <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Dark_Destiny\" target=\"_blank\">Dark Destiny</a> another anthology? Does it involve Sullivan or some of the San Francisco cast too?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1530498-review-dark-prince-by-keith-herber-the-first-vtm-novel?p=1530532#post1530532\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In a very real way, I feel like this book also does a decent job of reflecting how Fifth Edition should be played. It's a gritty street level series of adventures and events with a protagonist who is struggling against his Beast as well as the complicated politics of Kindred society.<br /> <br /> Sullivan doesn't WANT to scheme or do anything other than loyally serve. But loyalty means nothing if there's more to be had by betraying YOU.</div> </div> </div> </div>Though my current chronicle owes far more in style to Redemption and Bloodlines (very much by intent, since 4 of 6 PCs derive somehow from either game), you won't see me disagree on that.<br /> <br /> <br /> Anyway, looks like a good time to indulge into some purchases and nostalgia binge-reading.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 02-11-2024, 01:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-10T23:44:51-08:00","id":1530537,"title":"","content":"Crap. Typo. This is what happens when you post while editing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-11T00:11:27-08:00","id":1530538,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1530498-review-dark-prince-by-keith-herber-the-first-vtm-novel?p=1530537#post1530537\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Crap. Typo. This is what happens when you post while editing.</div> </div> </div> </div>It happens and i suspected anyway. No harm done, plus it lets us cite <b>another</b> White Wolf anthology that players old and new might enjoy delving into....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}